/T (For me, good joinery is not just about storage or finish. It is about how a room feels when you walk into it. The piece of furniture your eye is drawn to. The weight of a handle. The warmth of timber. The way a drawer opens. The feeling that something has been made specifically for the house, and for the people who live there.)
/E (For me, good joinery is not just about storage or finish. It is about how a room feels when you walk into it. The piece of furniture your eye is drawn to. The weight of a handle. The warmth of timber. The way a drawer opens. The feeling that something has been made specifically for the house, and for the people who live there.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
